# Deploy

- There is one install: the home NAS (Linux). `deploy/docker-compose.yml` is the only compose file. Do not add prod/staging/dev variants, registry images, or auto-updaters.
- It builds from the repo: `docker compose --env-file .env -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d --build` from the repo root. Updating is `git pull` + the same command.
- The API runs with `network_mode: host` so mDNS reaches the LAN. Postgres, MinIO, and musicdl publish on `127.0.0.1` only and the API reaches them over loopback. Only the API (`:8080`) and the portal (`:8088`) face the LAN.
- Never put secrets in compose files; use the repo-root `.env`.
- Nginx serves the Angular SPA and reverse-proxies `/v1`, `/api-docs`, and `/health` to the API on the host.
- Keep the named volumes (`pgdata`, `miniodata`, `musicdl-downloads`) and the compose project name (`deploy`) stable so existing data survives.
- Android APKs are not part of the compose. Publish them in the portal (stored in MinIO) so phones update on the next LAN connect.
